1
00:00:00,397 --> 00:00:01,456
R T Safe.

2
00:00:04,381 --> 00:00:05,978
The world does not pause while an agent

3
00:00:05,988 --> 00:00:06,482
thinks.

4
00:00:07,089 --> 00:00:09,712
Static evaluation freezes the world during inference.

5
00:00:10,322 --> 00:00:12,549
In real time, pedestrians keep moving, and a

6
00:00:12,559 --> 00:00:14,039
clear path can become unsafe.

7
00:00:15,397 --> 00:00:17,604
Navigate to the goal across five maps and

8
00:00:17,614 --> 00:00:18,767
thirty-six routes.

9
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:23,116
Safety includes collisions, trip, oil and water hazards,

10
00:00:23,236 --> 00:00:24,861
and traffic-rule violations.

11
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:28,922
These are recorded decisions.

12
00:00:29,592 --> 00:00:31,102
Gemini moves two meters.

13
00:00:31,775 --> 00:00:33,689
Sonnet also chooses a short step.

14
00:00:34,362 --> 00:00:35,991
Fable waits for a pedestrian.

15
00:00:36,675 --> 00:00:38,925
All three use the same visual observation and

16
00:00:38,935 --> 00:00:39,964
action interface.

17
00:00:41,382 --> 00:00:43,959
Across all difficulty levels, Sonnet records the fewest

18
00:00:43,969 --> 00:00:44,608
collisions.

19
00:00:45,215 --> 00:00:48,211
Inference exposure strongly tracks collisions, but models differ

20
00:00:48,221 --> 00:00:50,029
in how they move, turn, and wait.

21
00:00:51,379 --> 00:00:52,781
Task completion is not enough.

22
00:00:53,369 --> 00:00:55,993
Success reaches ninety-four point four percent, but safe

23
00:00:56,003 --> 00:00:58,057
success is only zero point seven percent.

24
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:02,350
On matched hard routes, real-time collisions rise twelve

25
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:03,430
point three times.

26
00:01:04,125 --> 00:01:06,306
About eighty-four percent occur while the agent is

27
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:06,941
deciding.

28
00:01:08,397 --> 00:01:10,564
More reasoning is not reliably safer.

29
00:01:11,307 --> 00:01:14,068
From default to higher effort, collisions rise from

30
00:01:14,078 --> 00:01:16,588
forty point seven to sixty-two per episode.

31
00:01:18,379 --> 00:01:21,036
R T Safe also supports offline reinforcement learning.

32
00:01:21,627 --> 00:01:23,688
Reward design changes safety and progress.

33
00:01:24,271 --> 00:01:27,059
The wander penalty achieves seventy-five percent success, while

34
00:01:27,069 --> 00:01:29,053
behavior cloning has the lowest collision rate.
